# E1/WP2: lld-native ADDRESS-LEVEL static parameter-slot reentrancy check and
# the versioned link-facts interface (IC-014; review round 2).  The legacy
# function-level diagnosis cannot see that two DIFFERENT leaf functions'
# parameter slots land on the same bytes, nor that ONE slot is reached from
# both contexts.  These cases pin the reviewed contract:
#   * both shapes are detected (different slots intersecting; one slot shared
#     from interleavable contexts) and a PROVEN violation fails the link by
#     default, with the exact shared range and per-slot access evidence;
#   * only CONFIRMED machine-level evidence may justify "proven": a control
#     relocation must sit on a real control opcode at a trusted instruction
#     boundary (a `mov`-immediate carrying R_MCS251_24 is not a call), and a
#     slot access must be the producer's confirmed 24-bit absolute address
#     materialization (`7E 18 mm ll` + `7A 1C hh 00`);
#   * a control target outside every function interval is an unknown, never a
#     crash; neither is a non-call R24;
#   * the structured result is authoritative: complete participating slot set,
#     per-slot access evidence, and the specific proving pair, all rendered
#     from the same records the facts interface publishes;
#   * coverage status is emitted on the success AND failure paths; severity
#     (off/warn/error) and coverage (allow/require) are separate axes;
#   * the external preemption contract is validated independently of both;
#   * requesting facts never changes any verdict, and facts are published in
#     every output mode (plain, placement audit, verify).
# The fixtures use the producer's real encodings and the real CRT; two cases
# additionally drive the REAL compiler (llc) from checked-in IR.

# RUN: rm -rf %t-seed && split-file %s %t-seed
# RUN: yaml2obj %S/../../../validation/mcs251-elf/runtime/crt-irq-v2.yaml -o %t.crt.o
# RUN: %python %S/Inputs/isr-v2flags.py %t.crt.o

# --- (a) proven address-level conflict: two different leaf slots in overlaid
# --- OSEG areas, one reached only from a registered ISR and one only from the
# --- foreground.  Exact shared range [0x0000,0x0002) (the lowest DSEG window
# --- is empty in this link), the proving pair, both sides' caller-write and
# --- callee-read evidence, and default rc=1 with no artifact.
# RUN: yaml2obj %t-seed/conflict.yaml -o %t.c.o
# RUN: %python %S/Inputs/isr-v2flags.py %t.c.o
# RUN: rm -f %t.c.elf
# RUN: not mcs251-lld %t.crt.o %t.c.o --area-start=HOME=0xff0000 \
# RUN:   --area-start=BOOT=0xff0500 --area-start=CSEG=0xff0700 \
# RUN:   --area-start=XINIT=0xff8000 -o %t.c.elf 2> %t.c.err
# RUN: FileCheck %s --check-prefix=CONFLICT < %t.c.err
# CONFLICT: error: ISR reentrancy: proven static parameter-slot contract violation: parameter slots are shared across the ISR and foreground execution contexts at [0x0000,0x0002)
# CONFLICT: error: ISR reentrancy:   proven pair: {{0x[0-9a-f]+}}:{{0x[0-9a-f]+}}:{{0x[0-9a-f]+}} / {{0x[0-9a-f]+}}:{{0x[0-9a-f]+}}:{{0x[0-9a-f]+}}
# CONFLICT: error: ISR reentrancy:   slot _fg_scale_PARM_2 [object {{[0-9]+}} section {{[0-9]+}} symbol {{[0-9]+}}] 0x0000 +2 in .mcs251.OSEG.3
# CONFLICT: error: ISR reentrancy:     by '_main' ({{.*}}, foreground context; writes slot before the call (caller side of the static-slot ABI, confirmed call))
# CONFLICT: error: ISR reentrancy:     by '_fg_scale' ({{.*}}, foreground context; reads slot at entry (callee side of the static-slot ABI))
# CONFLICT: error: ISR reentrancy:   slot _isr_scale_PARM_2 [object {{[0-9]+}} section {{[0-9]+}} symbol {{[0-9]+}}] 0x0000 +2 in .mcs251.OSEG.1
# CONFLICT: error: ISR reentrancy:     by '_irq1' ({{.*}}, ISR context; writes slot before the call (caller side of the static-slot ABI, confirmed call))
# CONFLICT: error: ISR reentrancy:     by '_isr_scale' ({{.*}}, ISR context; reads slot at entry (callee side of the static-slot ABI))
# CONFLICT: error: ISR reentrancy:   ISR context roots: _irq1
# CONFLICT: error: ISR reentrancy:   interleaving condition: registered ISR preempts foreground (default preemption contract)
# CONFLICT: error: ISR reentrancy:   evidence: slot accesses verified at trusted instruction boundaries; control transfers: confirmed opcodes, plus the frozen-CRT reset/boot chain platform contract
# CONFLICT: warning: ISR reentrancy: coverage status: open -
# CONFLICT-SAME: 1 address conflict group
# A hard failure leaves no success artifact.
# RUN: not test -e %t.c.elf

# --- (b) the SAME slot reached from both contexts (the review finding 1
# --- shape): one leaf whose static slot is written by an ISR-context caller
# --- and by a foreground caller.  This must be proven, not just reported as
# --- a function-level candidate.
# RUN: llc -mtriple=mcs251 -O0 -filetype=obj -mcs251-object-format=elf %S/Inputs/reentrancy-shared-slot.ll -o %t.shared.o
# RUN: not mcs251-lld %t.crt.o %t.shared.o --area-start=HOME=0xff0000 \
