# RUN:   --area-start=XINIT=0xff8000 -o %t.shared.elf 2> %t.shared.err
# RUN: FileCheck %s --check-prefix=SHARED-PROVEN < %t.shared.err
# SHARED-PROVEN: error: ISR reentrancy: proven static parameter-slot contract violation: one parameter slot is reached from interleavable contexts at [0x000c,0x000e)
# SHARED-PROVEN: error: ISR reentrancy:   proven pair: {{.*}} / {{.*}}
# SHARED-PROVEN: error: ISR reentrancy:     by '_timer0_isr' ({{.*}}, ISR context; writes slot before the call
# SHARED-PROVEN: error: ISR reentrancy:     by '_main' ({{.*}}, foreground context; writes slot before the call
# SHARED-PROVEN: error: ISR reentrancy:   interleaving condition: registered ISR preempts foreground

# --- (c) legal contrast, REAL compiler output: a function called from BOTH
# --- contexts that has NO static parameter slot (one argument) must NOT be
# --- reported as an address-level violation; the legacy candidate warning and
# --- a zero-conflict coverage status are all that appear.
