# --- (z1) ROUND-4: a VALID non-empty preemption contract must not bypass the
# --- publication path matrix.  The facts alias on the ELF's staging path is
# --- rejected in EVERY output mode (plain, placement report, verify), the
# --- old artifacts stay byte-identical, and the same command with a distinct
# --- facts path still succeeds.  R5 note: the contract names two DISTINCT
# --- ISR entries (`preempt _irq1 _irq2` on the two-ISR slotless fixture),
# --- so the success control does not depend on the rejected same-name
# --- pair handling of (z9).
