# The coverage state also loses the BOOT-chain carrier: with no kind=1 chain
# the two walker bodies are ordinary (undecodable, hand-written) code, so
# neither walker nor the module entry is contract-carried and the BOOT-chain
# evidence=4 edges disappear.  The kind=0 HOME trampoline survives (it is an
# independent, still-valid contract site), so the counts drop to: no kind=1
# chain site, one contract edge (reset -> paired BOOT entry), one contract
# context (that BOOT entry).
