# --- (z7) ROUND-5 finding 2: the DECIDING pair's roots, and per-pair root
# --- identity.  One two-argument function called from THREE registered
# --- ISRs: the same-slot group has six ordered (writer root, user root)
# --- combinations.  With only `_irq2/_irq3' declared the two established
# --- combinations and the four missing ones are each named with their OWN
# --- write root and use root; the A/B side lines and the facts roots_a/
# --- roots_b carry the DECIDING pair's roots only.  With `_irq1/_irq2' and
# --- `_irq2/_irq3' both declared (FOUR established combinations) the side
# --- lines still name exactly the deciding pair, never the union.
# RUN: llc -mtriple=mcs251 -O0 -filetype=obj -mcs251-object-format=elf %S/Inputs/reentrancy-three-isr.ll -o %t.f3.o
# RUN: not mcs251-lld %t.crt.o %t.f3.o --area-start=HOME=0xff0000 \
# RUN:   --area-start=BOOT=0xff0500 --area-start=CSEG=0xff0700 \
# RUN:   --area-start=XINIT=0xff8000 --isr-preemption-config=%t-seed/preempt-23.txt \
# RUN:   -o %t.f3a.elf 2> %t.f3a.err
# RUN: FileCheck %s --check-prefix=PAIR3-EST --implicit-check-not="A side ISR roots: _irq2 _irq3" --implicit-check-not="B side ISR roots: _irq2 _irq3" < %t.f3a.err
# The six per-pair lines, in evaluation order, each with its own roots.
# PAIR3-EST: proven static parameter-slot contract violation
# PAIR3-EST: pair {{0x[0-9a-f]+}}:{{0x[0-9a-f]+}}:{{0x[0-9a-f]+}} / {{0x[0-9a-f]+}}:{{0x[0-9a-f]+}}:{{0x[0-9a-f]+}} (write root _irq1; use root _irq2): missing ISR-vs-ISR preemption is not declared
# PAIR3-EST: pair {{0x[0-9a-f]+}}:{{0x[0-9a-f]+}}:{{0x[0-9a-f]+}} / {{0x[0-9a-f]+}}:{{0x[0-9a-f]+}}:{{0x[0-9a-f]+}} (write root _irq1; use root _irq3): missing ISR-vs-ISR preemption is not declared
# PAIR3-EST: pair {{0x[0-9a-f]+}}:{{0x[0-9a-f]+}}:{{0x[0-9a-f]+}} / {{0x[0-9a-f]+}}:{{0x[0-9a-f]+}}:{{0x[0-9a-f]+}} (write root _irq2; use root _irq1): missing ISR-vs-ISR preemption is not declared
# PAIR3-EST: pair {{0x[0-9a-f]+}}:{{0x[0-9a-f]+}}:{{0x[0-9a-f]+}} / {{0x[0-9a-f]+}}:{{0x[0-9a-f]+}}:{{0x[0-9a-f]+}} (write root _irq2; use root _irq3): established
# PAIR3-EST: pair {{0x[0-9a-f]+}}:{{0x[0-9a-f]+}}:{{0x[0-9a-f]+}} / {{0x[0-9a-f]+}}:{{0x[0-9a-f]+}}:{{0x[0-9a-f]+}} (write root _irq3; use root _irq1): missing ISR-vs-ISR preemption is not declared
# PAIR3-EST: pair {{0x[0-9a-f]+}}:{{0x[0-9a-f]+}}:{{0x[0-9a-f]+}} / {{0x[0-9a-f]+}}:{{0x[0-9a-f]+}}:{{0x[0-9a-f]+}} (write root _irq3; use root _irq2): established
# The side lines name the DECIDING pair only (anchored to the line end, so
# a union form cannot match).
# PAIR3-EST: A side ISR roots: _irq2{{$}}
# PAIR3-EST: B side ISR roots: _irq3{{$}}
# RUN: mcs251-lld %t.crt.o %t.f3.o --area-start=HOME=0xff0000 \
# RUN:   --area-start=BOOT=0xff0500 --area-start=CSEG=0xff0700 \
