# R5-r2: the diagnostic also names the contract file and PHYSICAL line, so a
# multi-line contract points at the offending row (see (z10)).
# SELF-PAIR: ISR preemption contract declares '_irq1' preempting itself at {{.*}}preempt-self.txt:1 (from '_irq1 _irq1'): a preemption pair must name two DISTINCT registered ISR entries

# --- (z10) ROUND-5 finding 3: repeating --isr-preemption-config is REJECTED.
# --- Before the fix the parser kept a single last-wins path while the PAIR
# --- SET accumulated, so `--isr-preemption-config=A --isr-preemption-config=B
# --- --link-facts=A` passed every mode's publication check and published the
# --- facts file over A -- a contract that had already been READ and had
# --- already contributed pairs to the analysis.  The regression pins:
# ---   * the reject happens BEFORE any artifact is published, in plain,
# ---     placement-report and verify modes alike -- so the ELF is absent and
# ---     neither the placement report nor the facts file is created;
# ---   * the contract file's bytes are unchanged (byte identity, not size);
# ---   * the SAME outcome when the two options are swapped, so neither
# ---     occurrence is privileged;
# ---   * the same for a repeated PATH (both occurrences name A), and for an
# ---     ALIAS of A with BOTH link shapes: a HARD link (a second name for
# ---     the same inode, `ln` without -s) and a SYMBOLIC link (`ln -s`);
# ---   * the exit status is EXACTLY 1 in every case, asserted with
# ---     expect-rc.py rather than lit's `not` helper (which only requires a
# ---     NON-ZERO status).  The rest of this file keeps `not`, so "the
# ---     persistent suite pins a non-zero exit" and "rc=1 was measured
# ---     here" are separate claims and must not be merged.
# --- A is a VALID non-empty contract and B is a comment-only contract, the
# --- exact pair of shapes from the finding.
# RUN: rm -rf %t-z10 && mkdir %t-z10 && cd %t-z10
# RUN: cp %t-seed/preempt-2.txt A.txt
# RUN: printf '# B: comments only\n' > B.txt
# RUN: cp A.txt A.orig
